id: schemas/node
title: "schema modules"
kind: schema-index
status: active
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Hold machine-valid state-substrate modules and explicitly labeled protocol
  drafts. Each schema is canonical only for its own version and kind.

holds:
  - statuses.v1.schema.json
  - event.v1.schema.json
  - materialized-state.v1.schema.json
  - state-snapshot.v1.schema.json
  - desire.v1.schema.json
  - target-condition.v1.schema.json
  - transition-intent.v1.schema.json
  - transition-result.v1.schema.json
  - state-update.v1.schema.json
  - living-snapshot.v1.schema.json
  - record-ref.v1.schema.json
  - record-event.v1.schema.json
  - record-proof-receipt.v1.schema.json
  - observation.v1.schema.json
  - projection-preference.v1.schema.json
  - question-proposal.v1.schema.json
  - art-brief.v1.schema.json
  - local-art-candidate.v1.schema.json
  - view-feedback.v1.schema.json
  - action-signature.v1.schema.json
  - execution-relationship.v1.schema.json
  - action-policy.v1.schema.json
  - reconciliation-batch.v1.schema.json
  - action-receipt.v1.schema.json
  - agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  - objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json
  - orientation-map.v0.1.schema.json
  - inquiry-selection-receipt.v0.1.schema.json
  - move-selection-receipt.v0.1.schema.json
  - choice-event.v0.1.schema.json

compatibility: >
  Legacy current/possible/desired fields remain readable at system boundaries.
  Canonical V1 records use attributed snapshots, optional targets, explicit
  authority, and separate transition intent/result.

module_boundary: >
  The @yawn/contracts package is the stable v1 constitution/runtime bundle.
  These root schemas are the parallel state-substrate v1 modules plus the
  experimental Agency Holarchy 0.2, Objective Holon 0.1, Orientation Map 0.1,
  Move Selection Receipt 0.1, and Choice Event 0.1 modules. Neither surface is
  described as the complete schema for every human-readable .yawn file.

observation_boundary: >
  Observation V1 is an accepted source-backed record that remains valid
  without a Target, Move, or Yawn. Record references let events and proof
  address observations and Git commits without adding ontology-specific
  foreign keys. Projection preferences affect Views only and preserve
  field-level provenance.

observation_proposal_boundary: >
  Question, Art Brief, local candidate, and Projection feedback records are
  closed proposal contracts around an exact Observation hash. They cannot
  accept themselves, apply preferences, publish, promote, or mutate canonical
  state. The tracked feedback fixture is synthetic; private exact text remains
  in a local receipt.

delegated_execution_boundary: >
  Execution Relationship V1 begins with an attributed owner/delegate edge,
  constrains every external effect with an exact Action Signature, records
  owner-decided reconciliation batches, and returns each consequence as an
  Action Receipt. Repeated clean receipts may create a policy proposal; only a
  rightful grantor can activate or widen reusable authority.

agency_holarchy_draft: >
  Draft 0.2 adds provider-neutral arena boundaries, one-parent holarchy,
  lateral relations, asynchronous turns, transitions, proof receipts, routing
  proposals, and structural-change receipts without redefining v1.

objective_holon_draft: >
  Draft 0.1 separates typed objective detection, principal ratification,
  objective-holding Yawns, sleeping bot bindings, activation receipts, and
  effect authority without redefining v1 or Agency Holarchy 0.2.

orientation_map_draft: >
  Draft 0.1 defines one nine-axis, attributed, source-backed orientation View,
  proposed presentation-fit hypotheses, and deterministic question-ranking
  inputs without making the map canonical state or preference semantic truth.
  Its inquiry-selection receipt closes the selected-question versus hold result,
  pins prompt and policy inputs, and remains non-authoritative View provenance.

choice_and_move_selection_draft: >
  Draft 0.1 gives typed identities to the recommendation and rightful-choice
  seams already implied by Transition Intent. A Move Selection Receipt is a
  replayable inferred proposal or hold, never choice or authority. A Choice
  Event records the rightful principal's selection, hold, or rejection and
  cannot grant effect authority by itself.

status_rule: >
  Modal, motivational, epistemic, lifecycle, authority, loop,
  axis-resolution, and presentation statuses are independent dimensions.

proof:
  command: "npm ci && npm test"
  status: contract-defined
